WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.530
In 2003, Hull was named
the worst town in Britain.

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.250
A major port, it had
suffered steady decline,

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.050
as its fishing industry
shrank from the 1970s.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.730
Then, in 2017, Hull
became UK City of Culture:

5
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.650
a chance to counter its negative image.

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.210
Around it, a wind-turbine
blade plant was pledged:

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.190
160 million pounds, and 1,000 jobs.

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.530
Years later, how could anyone
prove whether any of it worked?

9
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.330
In this mission, you'll sort
the evidence into four kinds:

10
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.230
economic, social, demographic
and environmental.

11
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.890
Then you'll read Hull's
own data across a decade,

12
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.590
and judge what really changed.

13
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.210
Your mission: decide how anyone could
prove whether a regeneration scheme has

14
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.010
worked.
